DATASET: BHARATTHERMAL-1, ODbL 1.0

The dataset is licensed under the Open Database License 1.0, in full and as one
database. `scripts/export_kaggle.py` builds the released files.

https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

The feature set contains a column copied from an OpenStreetMap attribute and a
column computed against OpenStreetMap geometry. OpenStreetMap is ODbL 1.0, which
requires share alike on a derivative database. Rather than argue whether this
dataset is a derivative database or a produced work, it is released under the same
licence as the source, which is correct under either reading.

What that means for anyone using it. You may copy, distribute, adapt and build on
the dataset, including commercially. If you publicly use an adapted version of the
database you must release that adaptation under ODbL 1.0 as well, and you must
attribute this dataset and the upstream sources listed below.

The cost of this choice is stated plainly: share alike propagates to your work. It
is the price of a licence position that needs no legal argument to defend, and it
was chosen deliberately over a split release that would have left the model
features permissive and the labels share alike.

Two consequences worth naming.

The NASA FIRMS, Global Energy Monitor and ESA WorldCover material in this dataset
is more permissively licensed upstream than ODbL requires. Distributing it here
under ODbL is allowed, and it does not restrict anyone from obtaining that material
from its original source under its original terms.

The distance to the nearest catalogued gas flare, derived from the EOG catalogue,
is not distributed in any form beyond coarse bands. That catalogue permits
attribution but does not confirm redistribution, and no choice of licence here
changes what its terms allow.

The console data feed under apps/console/public/data is a subset of this dataset
and carries the same terms.


UPSTREAM SOURCES AND THEIR TERMS

  NASA FIRMS                     active fire detections, free and open,
                                 attribution requested
  OpenStreetMap                  ODbL 1.0, attribution and share alike on a
                                 derivative database
  Global Energy Monitor          CC BY 4.0
  ESA WorldCover                 CC BY 4.0
  Copernicus Sentinel-2          free with attribution. Contains modified
                                 Copernicus Sentinel data 2024
  EOG, Colorado School of Mines  attribution required, redistribution not
                                 confirmed

Full attribution text is in README.md.


